# Button states

Style every `<button>` for all six states. Use tokens from `globals.css` only.

| State | Selector | Where it applies |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Rest | the class | every viewport |
| Hover | `:hover` | only inside `@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)` |
| Focus | `:focus-visible` | every viewport; theme outline, keyboard only |
| Press | `:active` | every viewport, including touch |
| Disabled | `:disabled` | every viewport; quieter text, `cursor: not-allowed`, even if none are disabled yet |
| Chosen | `[aria-current]`, `[aria-pressed="true"]`, or `[aria-expanded="true"]` | every viewport; stays after the pointer lifts |

Do not use `:hover` as the only feedback. A finger never hovers.

One example:

```css
.action:active,
.action[aria-pressed="true"] {
  color: var(--color-text-primary);
}

.action:focus-visible {
  outline: 1px solid var(--color-secondary);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}

.action:disabled {
  color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
  cursor: not-allowed;
}

@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
  .action:hover {
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }
}
```
